1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,860
I feel a lot better knowing it's you.

3
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,440
I've been in the bathroom this whole time.

4
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,920
I think... there's no way I can go to the duel now.

5
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,020
You're just scared, so you're faking it!

6
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,420
Me? Scared? Scared of what?

7
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,350
Shawn.

8
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,300
You actually look pretty good dressed up as a girl.

9
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Episode 16

10
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,910
Shawn played a crucial role

11
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,900
in all of this.

12
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,340
Everyone saw it.

13
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,250
Hold on, Coach. Can I have a word with you in private?

14
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,580
Alright.

15
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:07,740
Coach, since you've already acknowledged my contribution,

16
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,180
could I maybe ask for

17
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:11,580
a very tiny little favor?

18
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,970
Sure. As long as it's not joining the
School Team, anything goes.

19
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,300
Coach, you're... you're not

20
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,220
backing me into a corner here, are you?

21
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:25,020
Shawn, you don't have any Practical Skills.

22
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,990
If you were on the School Team,
how would you even Compete?

23
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,260
You've got it all wrong, Coach.

24
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,180
My love for Yo-Yos

25
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,580
goes way beyond just competing in Matches.

26
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:38,940
Competing is just a fleeting moment of glory.

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,860
But my passion for Yo-Yos,

28
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,740
that's an eternal wellspring in my soul.

29
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:48,540
I promise, as long as you let me stay with the Team,

30
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,940
I'd even be happy doing chores.

31
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:57,180
I'll think about it.

32
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,580
Everyone's doing homework.

33
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,020
Hey, Coach Tony.

34
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,460
Coach Tony.

35
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,860
I have an announcement to make.

36
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,740
From today on, Shawn officially becomes

37
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,260
the Logistics Minister and Theory Guide for Jianghai Team.

38
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,940
Let's give him a warm welcome!

39
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,180
What's a "Logistics Minister"?

40
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,030
That means he's in charge of sweeping up for us,

41
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,900
cooking, doing laundry, and all that.

42
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,340
Basically, all the stuff we're too busy practicing to do.

43
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,920
All that falls on the Logistics Minister.

44
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,140
Then what's a "Theory Guide"?

45
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,500
That's just someone with no skills
who only knows how to talk.

46
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,380
In other words, the guy in charge of talking big.

47
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,700
There are limits to joking, you know.

48
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,100
No worries, no worries at all.

49
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,020
Coach, I'm already more than satisfied.

50
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:02,940
Sit down.

51
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,300
I also have another huge piece of good news

52
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,740
to share with everyone.

53
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,140
The funding issue for Jianghai Team...

54
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,580
has been completely resolved!

55
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:13,980
So that means no more sleeping in tents!

56
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,390
Exactly!

57
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,860
That's awesome!

58
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:21,660
And also, we'll be getting new Team Uniforms!

59
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,510
Really? That's great! That's amazing!

60
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,980
Coach, you're like a magician!

61
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:28,380
You just snap your fingers and poof—
funding and uniforms appear!

62
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,180
Honestly, I really lucked out this time.

63
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,100
I thought all hope was lost, too.

64
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,470
But just as I was heading to the very last Company,

65
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,430
On my way there,

66
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,900
I ran into my old Classmate Zhang Lu at the front door.

67
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,710
My old Classmate—last time I went to his company,

68
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,150
his Secretary made a mistake

69
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,270
and gave me a cup of calming tea.

70
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:51,930
Tony!

71
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,780
Oh, Zhang Lu!

72
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,700
How come you never come see me anymore?

73
00:04:57,640 --> 00:05:00,060
Come see you? After that tea you gave me last time?

74
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,460
Oh, you mean that calming tea?

75
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,820
That was my Secretary, Lily.
She accidentally gave you my tea.

76
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,220
Ah, forget it, forget it.

77
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,580
Anyway, regarding the funding and the Uniforms—
I've already approved them!

78
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,460
What? Approved already?

79
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:15,500
Yes

80
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:19,230
I really didn't expect it.
I thought you didn't want anything to do with me anymore.

81
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,700
Come on, old friend.
You're selling me way too short.

82
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:21,890
Really, really, old pal.

83
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,020
You have no idea how happy I am.

84
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:28,860
I'm so thrilled.
You really came through for us in a time of need.

85
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:32,110
Well, that's that settled.

86
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,140
Everything's taken care of now.

87
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:37,500
This is what you call
"Surviving a disaster guarantees future fortune!"

88
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:39,900
Why do you have to say it like that?

89
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,780
I think the Jianghai Team's luck is finally turning around.

90
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:46,140
I'm sure winning the Championship won't be a problem for us!

91
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,940
Alright. Now, I declare...

92
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,460
To celebrate the fact

93
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,380
that all of the Jianghai Team's problems have been resolved,

94
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,780
tomorrow night, it's my treat!

95
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:57,660
How about we all have a nice, big feast?

96
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,100
Yeah!

97
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:03,420
The thing I've been dreaming about has finally come true!

98
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,780
I also want to give a special reward to two of our heroes:

99
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,220
Shawn and Leo.

100
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,620
Tell me, what do you two want to eat?

101
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:15,390
When it comes to material things,
I've never really cared much about them.

102
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,880
There you go again. If you won't answer, then I will!

103
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,700
This is none of your business.

104
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,580
Leo, what do you want to eat the most?

105
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:27,870
It's been ages since I've had a Cheese Sandwich.

106
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,340
That's what I'm really craving right now.

107
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,220
Cheese? That stuff is so gross.

108
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,140
Just the smell of it makes me wanna gag.

109
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,580
It's not for you anyway.

110
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:43,740
Hmm, that Cheese request might be a little tricky.

111
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,140
I don't think the Base kitchen

112
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,060
can make Cheese Sandwiches like that.

113
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,460
But there is Cheese in the Kitchen!

114
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,420
How do you know that?

115
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,300
You must've seen it that time you snuck into the Kitchen.

116
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:55,740
Don't bring that up again!

117
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:59,100
I take the long way around just to
avoid walking past the Kitchen now.

118
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,900
I've been looking all over for you. So here you are.

119
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,220
It's been a while since I've watched a sunset.

120
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,460
Leo, I was wrong about you.

121
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,860
I shouldn't have said all those things to you.

122
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,220
It was just a misunderstanding.

123
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,660
I didn't take it to heart.

124
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:02,460
Honestly, I shouldn't have doubted you.

125
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:06,780
I should've realised sooner that you had your own plan.

126
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,140
It's so rare to see you all fired up like that.

127
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,020
I actually thought it was kinda cute.

128
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:19,260
Actually, I should apologize to you all, too.

129
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,140
To keep things secret and throw off the Masked Guy,

130
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,980
I had to use reverse psychology that
day and push Mickey into the duel.

131
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,380
He must've been so mad at me.

132
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,780
He'd never be mad at you.

133
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,220
He worships you way too much.

134
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:38,460
Actually, both Mickey and I have
always looked up to you a lot.

135
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,620
Mini, I've put together a set of moves

136
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,540
specifically to counter your Light Wheel Technique.

137
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,500
Really?

138
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,390
Would you be willing to learn it?

139
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,860
Of course I would!

140
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,740
I always thought you didn't want to teach me anything.

141
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:58,620
I just wanted you to figure things out on your own first.

142
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,500
After all, true Yo-Yo feeling is something
you have to discover for yourself.

143
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,460
I know.

144
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:04,380
After watching you,

145
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,300
I think you're better suited to practicing techniques

146
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:07,710
that rely on skill and finesse

147
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,700
rather than just brute force.

148
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,940
Like this move, Golden Serpent Dance-

149
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,500
Captain.

150
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,860
Looks like Leo's trying to stage a comeback.

151
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:33,630
Look at him, he's so totally full of himself.

152
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,460
Jianghai Team! Victory!

153
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:09,660
Keep your release steady.

154
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,380
Coach!

155
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,660
Keep practicing, everyone!

156
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,940
You needed me for something?

157
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:28,380
I wanted to chat with you.

158
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,220
Mark, you take over and keep them practicing.

159
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,180
Got it.

160
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,500
Jianghai Team! Free practice!

161
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:40,350
What?

162
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:40,860
What?

163
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:45,180
We rented this platform as soon as we got to the Base.

164
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:46,590
A while back,

165
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,020
we had to stop using it because our funds were tight.

166
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:50,940
But now that Training's back on,

167
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,860
how could it possibly cause any conflict with your Team?

168
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,300
Exactly.

169
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:57,180
When we first arrived at the Base,
we rented this platform too.

170
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,060
We've been Training here the whole time.

171
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,500
You can't just say you're resuming Training

172
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:02,940
and expect there to be no conflict.

173
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,740
Well, then it sounds like the Base Management messed up.

174
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,620
How could they rent the same platform to both of our Teams?

175
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,030
They didn't mess up.

176
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,020
The Contract clearly states

177
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,940
that each Team gets to use it for half the day.

178
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,380
Well, then there's no problem.

179
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,820
I only need to train here in the Morning.

180
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,740
The rest of the time is all yours.

181
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,580
You sure know how to pick your times, don't you?

182
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:26,460
The reason I came was to talk to you about this.

183
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,380
We'd like to use it for Training in the mornings.

184
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,780
You can have it the rest of the time.

185
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:35,070
Our Team has a schedule.
Where we are, what time we train, what we practice—

186
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,060
it's all planned out.

187
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,980
Why should I have to mess up my whole plan for you?

188
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,350
Don't use your "plan" as an excuse to push me around.

189
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,340
Everyone knows it's cooler in the morning.

190
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,260
The rest of the day is just blazing hot sun.

191
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:46,140
Oh. I honestly hadn't thought about that.

192
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,060
Yeah, right.

193
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:49,980
Wait a minute.

194
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:54,300
So your Players don't want
to train in the sun, but mine should?

195
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,700
Why do you have to be so difficult about this?

196
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,100
Don't you know anything about "ladies first"?

197
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:02,460
This has nothing to do with "ladies first."

198
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,860
Back when you were Training for
sprints at the Sports Academy,

199
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,270
you weren't afraid of the sun.

200
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:09,180
Now, years after graduation,
suddenly you're scared of a little sun?

201
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,100
People change, you know.

202
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,950
Didn't you used to throw Shotput?

203
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,900
Now you're throwing Yo-Yos around.

204
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,840
How ridiculous is that.

205
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Ridiculous?

206
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,100
Okay, yeah, I used to throw Shotput.

207
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,420
But throwing a Shotput and throwing a Yo-Yo—

208
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,340
they're still kinda related, right?

209
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,190
But a Sprint Coach coming to teach Yo-Yo?

210
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,140
Now that is what I call ridiculous.

211
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,800
So I'm ridiculous, is that it?

212
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:40,350
Just wait until our Chengnan Team wins the Championship.

213
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,300
Then you won't be laughing so hard.

214
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:48,060
A woman who's always so Competitive
lacks any real tenderness.

215
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,460
She stops being a real woman.

216
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,860
You were like this back at the Academy,

217
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,260
and after all these years, you haven't changed a bit.

218
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,000
Fine...

219
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,580
So I'm not very ladylike.

220
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,500
But tell me, back at the Academy,

221
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,590
who was it that wouldn't stop chasing after me?

222
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,980
Keep your voice down, okay?

223
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,620
Okay, fine, I admit it. I did chase after you back then.

224
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,500
But that was when I was young and stupid.

225
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,900
If it were now? Hah!

226
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,300
If it were now, you'd have even less of a chance.

227
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,660
You're a grown man, and you
still love arguing with women.

228
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,510
You never give an inch.

229
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,980
No consideration at all.

230
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,820
Those are the marks of a petty little man.

231
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:30,780
You got that?

232
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:34,140
Hey, don't you go slapping labels like "little man" on me.

233
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,020
These days, it's all about equality.

234
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,460
There's no "ladies first."

235
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:45,180
There is absolutely no way Jianghai Team
is giving up this platform.

236
00:14:53,690 --> 00:14:56,220
This is great! It's all ours now!

237
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,140
Coach Sarah, you're amazing!

238
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,920
You finally kicked Jianghai Team out of here!

239
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,420
That Coach Tony guy.

240
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:07,230
Coach, does this mean we get to use
this place every morning from now on?

241
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:10,140
That's right. Now hurry up and train!
Don't waste any time!

242
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:24,540
Baby's  Cradle!

243
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,420
Focus on the catch!

244
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,220
Magic Glove!

245
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:39,900
Magical Ball!

246
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:51,420
Oh man, I'm dying of heat!

247
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,340
Scaling the Summit!

248
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:57,180
Eiffel Tower!

249
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Stop,

250
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:11,580
Everyone take a break up in the Tower!

251
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:41,820
I just went to the bathroom and saw
Chengnan Team over there chilling in the shade.

252
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,180
They've got iced drinks, and even green bean soup.

253
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,790
Man, that looks so nice.

254
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:49,020
What can we do about it?

255
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:50,940
They already finished their morning Training

256
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,820
while it was still nice and cool out.

257
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:55,740
So why couldn't we train there in the morning?

258
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,660
when its nice and cool.

259
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,060
How should I know? Go ask the Coach yourself.

260
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,910
Even if you did, it wouldn't change anything.

261
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:05,820
The Coach would just say it's to strengthen our willpower.

262
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:24,540
Let's see how long they can keep acting so smug.

263
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,940
It's Zoe.

264
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,340
Tell her I'm not here.

265
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,460
Zoe!

266
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,380
Coach Tony! Where's Matthew?

267
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,300
He's around here somewhere. Let me check for you.

268
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,660
Matthew! Matthew! You in there?

269
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,060
Coach, Matthew isn't here.

270
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,900
He was just here a second ago. That's weird.

271
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,780
I brought you guys some green bean soup.

272
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,190
If you see him,

273
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,660
just let him know I stopped by, okay?

274
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,580
Okay. Thanks.

275
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,940
Does your Coach Sarah know you came here?

276
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,860
She's the one who sent me!

277
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:06,300
Thanks.

278
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:08,470
Alright, well, thank your Coach Sarah
for me when you get back.

279
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,150
Okay!

280
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,550
Okay, Coach Tony! Goodbye!

281
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,540
Goodbye.

282
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:24,110
Alright, everyone! Have some green bean soup to cool down!

283
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,430
Yes! Awesome! I'm dying of thirst here!

284
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,420
It's green bean soup!

285
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,300
Gimme a bowl! Gimme one!

286
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,660
Matthew! I thought you said you weren't here?

287
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,580
I'm here, I'm here! Why wouldn't I be?

288
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,020
He's just scared of running into Zoe.

289
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:39,900
What's there to be scared of?

290
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,190
She brought us green bean soup, not poison.

291
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:44,820
Mark! You guys come have some too!

292
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,980
Coach, we're not thirsty. You guys go ahead.

293
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,820
We're not drinking anything that comes from Chengnan Team.

294
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,350
You needed something?

295
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,950
You just finished training and you're
already looking for Mini to practice more?

296
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:14,940
Don't you ever get tired?

297
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:17,340
It's fine if you're not tired,

298
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,260
but Mini might be.

299
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,180
If she's tired, she doesn't have to come.

300
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,580
That's something you should be asking her.

301
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,470
As Captain, I want you to put an end

302
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:27,420
to this kind of private training, immediately.

303
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:28,860
That's our personal time.

304
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,740
We can spend it however we want.

305
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:41,820
Hey! Stay away from Mini! You got that?

306
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,160
See? As long as that guy is around,

307
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:51,420
your Authority as Captain doesn't mean a single thing.

308
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,980
Attention! Dismissed!

309
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:10,620
Where's the Coach? Where'd he go?

310
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:13,020
Probably just went to the bathroom.

311
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,940
All you ever think about is the bathroom.

312
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:21,630
Leo, do you think you could give me some pointers too?

313
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:23,580
I feel like my Technique's been stuck in a rut lately.

314
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:24,540
Sure.

315
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:25,980
Just list out the things you're struggling with,

316
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,390
and I'll take a look for you.

317
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:29,340
Leo! We've got questions for you too!

318
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:31,260
We were just worried you wouldn't have time for us.

319
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,180
Did I ever say I didn't have time?

320
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:36,540
I was just a little concerned,
since everyone wants to ask you for help.

321
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,900
Leo hasn't even gotten around to helping me yet!

322
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,820
You guys should be getting in line behind me!

323
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:44,220
Mickey, don't be so selfish.

324
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,140
All theories are meant for the public good,

325
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,060
not someone's personal private property.

326
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:51,420
I don't want your theories! I just want Leo's advice!

327
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,790
Leo's advice is a part of my theories.

328
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,780
Advice is advice!

329
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,660
Every time you start talking about your theories,
my head feels like it's gonna explode!

330
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,500
So shallow. Just so shallow.
You truly lack any real understanding.

331
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,580
Look at Leo, acting like he's the Sun or something.

332
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,940
And everyone's just circling around
him like a bunch of Planets.

333
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,700
What, does he think he's the Captain now?

